WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:14.805
"Long ago," said Clan Mother, "the People of the Longhouse were always fighting.

2
00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:18.143
Mohawk warriors killed Cayuga.

3
00:00:18.144 --> 00:00:22.539
Oneida killed Seneca.

4
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.575
Too many people were dying.

5
00:00:25.576 --> 00:00:28.143
Too many people were crying.

6
00:00:28.144 --> 00:00:34.029
The Onondaga chief, Tadodaho, was very cruel and wild.

7
00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:37.280
His hair was full of snakes.

8
00:00:37.281 --> 00:00:41.622
One day a spirit appeared to a young Indian woman.

9
00:00:41.623 --> 00:00:48.279
The spirit told her, 'Your son will plant the Tree of Peace at Onondaga.'

10
00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.070
Her son was Deganawidah.

11
00:00:53.071 --> 00:00:56.600
Deganawidah grew into a young man.

12
00:00:56.601 --> 00:01:00.406
One day, he took his mother to a tree on a hill.

13
00:01:00.407 --> 00:01:05.364
'Mother, you must come to this tree every year,' he said.

14
00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.018
'Cut the tree.

15
00:01:07.019 --> 00:01:11.901
If blood flows, I have failed in my journey for peace.

16
00:01:11.902 --> 00:01:16.936
But if sap flows, I am alive and doing well.'

17
00:01:16.937 --> 00:01:21.748
Deganawidah made an amazing canoe out of white stone.

18
00:01:21.749 --> 00:01:25.683
He crossed the river into Onondaga land.

19
00:01:25.684 --> 00:01:29.217
He found a friend there―Hiawatha.

20
00:01:29.218 --> 00:01:35.678
The name Hiawatha means 'the one who combs,'" said Clan Mother.

21
00:01:35.679 --> 00:01:38.882
"Combs what?" asked Vinnie.

22
00:01:38.883 --> 00:01:44.811
"Combs the snakes from Tadodaho's hair," explained Clan Mother.

23
00:01:44.812 --> 00:01:49.400
"Someday, Hiawatha would calm the wild chief.

24
00:01:49.401 --> 00:01:54.417
Hiawatha and Deganawidah went to the land of the Mohawks.

25
00:01:54.418 --> 00:01:58.434
But no one there believed in his journey for peace.

26
00:01:58.435 --> 00:02:03.835
So Deganawidah climbed a very tall tree by a deep river.

27
00:02:03.836 --> 00:02:06.707
'Cut down this tree,' he said.

28
00:02:06.708 --> 00:02:10.906
'If I live, you will know my words are true.'

29
00:02:10.907 --> 00:02:13.748
The Mohawks did as he said."

30
00:02:13.749 --> 00:02:17.340
"Did he die?" interrupted Vinnie.

31
00:02:17.341 --> 00:02:20.105
"Hush," Clan Mother said.

32
00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:23.678
"The next day, the Mohawks found Deganawidah.

33
00:02:23.679 --> 00:02:25.402
He was alive.

34
00:02:25.403 --> 00:02:28.899
The Mohawks believed his message of peace.

35
00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:33.704
Hiawatha and Deganawidah went into Oneida land.

36
00:02:33.705 --> 00:02:37.819
The Oneida people were great friends of the Mohawks.

37
00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:41.162
So they quickly joined in the peace journey.

38
00:02:41.163 --> 00:02:45.010
Soon the Cayuga and the Seneca joined too.

39
00:02:45.011 --> 00:02:50.681
They all became Deganawidah's people," said Clan Mother.

40
00:02:50.682 --> 00:02:56.009
"What happened to the man with snakes in his hair?" Vinnie asked.

41
00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:59.954
"Patience," Clan Mother smiled.

42
00:02:59.955 --> 00:03:04.279
"The four nations now went to see Tadodaho.

43
00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:09.740
'We are to be united as Iroquois,' declared Deganawidah.

44
00:03:09.741 --> 00:03:14.135
'Why should I join you?' Tadodaho roared.

45
00:03:14.136 --> 00:03:17.693
'Onondaga is powerful on its own!'

46
00:03:17.694 --> 00:03:24.491
'But think how strong you would be if all of us were one people,' said Deganawidah.

47
00:03:24.492 --> 00:03:28.700
'If you agree, you will be head chief.'

48
00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:31.830
So Tadodahhoh agreed.

49
00:03:31.831 --> 00:03:35.430
Hiawatha combed the snakes from his hair.

50
00:03:35.431 --> 00:03:40.668
And there, in Onondaga, Deganawidah planted a tree.

51
00:03:40.669 --> 00:03:43.979
Its roots spread all over the earth.

52
00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:49.701
People everywhere who wanted peace could follow the roots to its source:

53
00:03:49.702 --> 00:03:52.072
the Tree of Peace.

54
00:03:52.073 --> 00:03:59.066
'Above this tree I place the eagle that can spy out danger,' said Deganawidah.

55
00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:01.954
'It will prepare you for battles.'

56
00:04:01.955 --> 00:04:07.278
Deganawidah also placed antlers on the heads of fifty chiefs.

57
00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:11.346
They would be the ones to rule the Five Nations.

58
00:04:11.347 --> 00:04:14.606
Then he made a promise to his people.

59
00:04:14.607 --> 00:04:19.335
'Call my name and I will return,' said Deganawidah.

60
00:04:19.336 --> 00:04:23.735
And that is how the Five Nations became united."

61
00:04:23.736 --> 00:04:33.501
Clan Mother dropped her head to her chest and closed her eyes.
